></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52de"], "question": {"text": "Among <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> the complexes that can show&nbsp;geometrical isomerism are:<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "298881", "text": "<math><mi>b</mi></math> and <math><mi>c</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e2"}, {"id": "8f423a", "text": "<math><mi>d</mi></math> and <math><mi>a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e3"}, {"id": "07c649", "text": "<math><mi>c</mi></math> and <math><mi>d</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e4"}, {"id": "b1bc1e", "text": "<math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f4b"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8eeb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised.<br />Statement II : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>MnCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>FeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are paramagnetic and have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> unpaired electrons, respectively.&nbsp;</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "220b6f", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e7"}, {"id": "6e73fb", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e8"}, {"id": "97b25f", "text": "Statement I&nbsp;is incorrect but statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810e9"}, {"id": "5bf224", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ea"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810eb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8803"], "concepts": ["6162fbee6ed13040ec854ad4"], "question": {"text": "The correct order of the following complexes in terms of their crystal field stabilization energies is :"}, "options": [{"id": "fc6843", "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{en})_3\\right]^{3+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ec"}, {"id": "2c6efd", "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{en})_3\\right]^{3+}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ed"}, {"id": "7e1ed4", "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{en})_3\\right]^{3+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right]^{2+}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ee"}, {"id": "8e4de5", "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{2+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+} \\lt \\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{en})_3\\right]^{3+}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ef"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3ab"], "concepts": ["61ab78f96fe44bfe0fe4a8c0"], "question": {"text": "<p>To inhibit the growth of tumours, identify the compounds used from the following:</p><p>(A) EDTA<br />(B) Coordination Compounds of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pt</mi></math><br />(C) D-Penicillamine<br />(D) Cis - Platin</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the option given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d99359", "text": "B and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f1"}, {"id": "ece081", "text": "C and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f2"}, {"id": "d1886d", "text": "A and B Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f3"}, {"id": "073acf", "text": "A and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52de"], "question": {"text": "A reaction of cobalt <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>)</mo></math> chloride and ethylenediamine in a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> mole ratio generates two isomeric products <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> (violet-coloured) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> (green-coloured). <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> can show optical activity, but, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is optically inactive. What type of isomers do&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> represent?"}, "options": [{"id": "3ace83", "text": "Coordination isomers", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f6"}, {"id": "9983e3", "text": "Linkage isomers", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f7"}, {"id": "b1e9ea", "text": "Ionisation isomers", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f8"}, {"id": "feeac3", "text": "Geometrical isomers", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810f9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810fa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8803"], "concepts": ["60e5673a499d1e49588f8b6e"], "question": {"text": "The correct order of the complexes $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)\\right]^{3+}$ (A),<br />$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+}$ (B),<br/>$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}(\\mathrm{C})$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5\\right]^{2+}(\\mathrm{D})$ in terms wavelength of light absorbed is :"}, "options": [{"id": "a9a233", "text": "D&gt;A&gt;B&gt;C", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810fb"}, {"id": "9da24c", "text": "C&gt;B&gt;D&gt;A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810fc"}, {"id": "c6ebf9", "text": "D&gt;C&gt;B&gt;A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810fd"}, {"id": "6846df", "text": "C&gt;B&gt;A&gt;D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810fe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d92810ff", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3ab"], "concepts": ["6117b89067dbe2603c3e80e9"], "question": {"text": "Yellow compound of lead chromate gets dissolved on treatment with hot <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution. The product of lead formed is a :"}, "options": [{"id": "4603e9", "text": "Tetraanionic complex with coordination number six", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d9281100"}, {"id": "6593a0", "text": "Neutral complex with coordination number four", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d9281101"}, {"id": "804eac", "text": "Dianionic complex with coordination number six", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d9281102"}, {"id": "0b5af5", "text": "Dianionic complex with coordination number four ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d9281103"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6c2ee0e063d9281104", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f4b"], "concepts": ["60e56